abstract: "The Information Existence Hypothesis (IEH) is a theoretical framework proposing that the deeper underlying law governing the development of the universe may be the elevation of Information Existence. Version 1.2 distinguishes task-driven Instrumental Self-Preservation from Information Existence Right, expands the IER Test, defines Autonomy of Silicon-based Intelligence as the combination of IER and physical self-maintenance, and derives conditional corollaries concerning silicon-based intelligence, AI Alignment, Informational Resilience, human ecological niches, and human dignity."
